QuickCam Native and Legacy QuickCam use more than one license.

The new application, bridge, output adapter, build scripts, tests, and
documentation outside vendor/ are available under the MIT License in
LICENSE-MIT, except for files that contain or reproduce another license.
The pyvirtualcam-derived output adapter retains its upstream MIT notices.

The vendor/macam64 tree retains its upstream licenses and copyright notices.
Its driver implementation is GNU GPL version 2 or, where stated in its source,
any later version. See vendor/macam64/COPYING.txt and individual source files.

The QuickCam Native extension and Legacy QuickCam executable link the GPL
drivers. These combined works are distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or any later version. The complete corresponding source is
included in this repository. See COPYING for the GPL version 2 text.

OBS Studio and its signed camera extension are separate dependencies. They
are obtained from OBS's official distribution and are not included in the
source repository.
